  "title": "Phase 4c piano: in tune, ringing, in the band",
  "intro": "The first family tuning set. Your c02 note said the piano choir 'sounds like a broken detune piano'. Measured: the notes themselves are in tune within a few cents, but every monk's small vibrato runs on its own, so a chord's intervals keep swinging. A new helper key locks the monks of a chord together. The piano notes also die much sooner than Gervill's. Three tests: chords, single lines, and the piano in a small band at your live balance.",
