    {
      "id": "chords",
      "title": "Piano chords: in tune?",
      "question": "Piano part alone (block chords, pedalled arpeggios, a long chord), 4 monks: which sound out of tune or detuned?",
      "notes": "Each monk's vibrato floor (\u00b10.2 st, the wobble that keeps Delay Lama alive) runs on its own, so the intervals of a chord swing by up to ~75 cents. 'Locked' makes every monk of a chord wobble together (new helper key vibrato.lock), so the intervals stay within ~10 cents and the chord wobbles as one. The tuning between notes is only 1-2 cents off (measured), so nothing else changes. Every clip at Gervill's loudness; blind mode is worth it.",
